Subject: Remove the null handler check from threaded dispatch

What this does
  Gives every register opcode a threaded-table entry. Opcodes that are not
  threaded return to the monolithic loop through a small trampoline.

Why we need it
  The interpreter tested the handler pointer on every dispatch to distinguish
  threaded opcodes from the remaining monolithic opcodes. That test is on the
  hot path for every register instruction.

What it adds
  A shared opcode list builds both the handler table and the threaded-eligibility
  table, keeping dispatch eligibility independent from handler pointer values.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

